# Find a mark
@scenario office_lesson_08
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg office]
[char pip global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show pip desk point]
pip: I need to stand beside the window. Watch which part of the frame stays still.
[if !tutorial_still]
[move pip desk stride-a-right exprdur=0]
[move pip window ease_in_out_cubic 740]
[wait 180]
[move pip window stride-b-right exprdur=0]
[wait 180]
[move pip window stride-c-right exprdur=0]
[wait 180]
[move pip window stride-b-right exprdur=0]
[wait 200]
[move pip window neutral exprdur=90]
[endif]
[if tutorial_still]
[show pip desk point]
pip: The window is my second mark. In reduced motion I point to it from here.
[else]
pip: Here is my window mark. Notice where the desk sits in the frame.
[endif]
[if !tutorial_still]
[move pip window stride-a-left exprdur=0]
[move pip desk ease_out_cubic 560]
[wait 140]
[move pip desk stride-b-left exprdur=0]
[wait 140]
[move pip desk stride-c-left exprdur=0]
[wait 140]
[move pip desk stride-b-left exprdur=0]
[wait 140]
[move pip desk point exprdur=90]
[endif]
pip: Back at the desk. Edit the window position or the duration of the first move, then replay.
@label check
pip: What lets an actor move without replacing the set?
> A new stage preset. -> retry
> A character position. -> correct
@label retry
[show pip desk curious]
pip: Character positions belong to the actor. Give it another try.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show pip desk cheer]
pip: Character positions belong to the actor.
> Finish this lesson -> return_hub
> Try the lesson again -> start
@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_08]
[flag tutorial_done_08]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_2]
